.TH SNMPDIGGER 1 "2026-09-04" "snmpdigger" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snmpdigger \- fancy TUI SNMP browser, live grapher and network discovery tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snmpdigger
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger discover
.RI { cidr | \-\-asn\ n | \-\-local }
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger walk
.I host
.RI [ oid ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger get
.I host
.I oid
.RI [ oid ... ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger monitor
.I host
.I oid
.RI [ oid ... ]
.RI [ \-\-interval\ n ]
.RI [ \-\-delta ]
.br
.B snmpdigger identify
.I host
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger config
.RI { path | show }
.br
.B snmpdigger version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snmpdigger
is a terminal application for exploring SNMP agents.
.PP
Run with no arguments it starts in full\-screen TUI mode, opening on the
Discovery tab.  The connection dialog is never forced: press
.B c
(or select a discovered host) to enter the target host, port, SNMP version and
the matching credentials (community string for v1/v2c, or user / security level
/ auth and privacy parameters for v3).  Once connected it walks the MIB/OID tree
and lets you browse it in a searchable, filterable, sortable list showing the
numeric OID, the resolved human\-readable name, the type and the live value.
Values are polled continuously on an adjustable interval.
.PP
Tabs: Discovery, System (device fingerprinting), Interfaces (a live IF\-MIB
dashboard with per\-port bit/s and utilisation), Browser, Graph (line, bar,
gauge, sparkline, big\-number or heatmap), Watch (a persistent pin\-board of
objects), Catalog (an offline MIB module/object reference plus on\-demand MIB
download) and Settings.  The
.B discover
sub\-command and tab sweep for SNMP\-speaking hosts by IPv4 CIDR range, by AS
number
.RB ( \-\-asn ,
prefixes resolved via RIPEstat), or across the host's local networks
.RB ( \-\-local ).
Settings persist to
.IR ~/.config/snmpdigger/config.yaml .
.PP
The sub\-commands provide non\-interactive access to the same engine for scripting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-community " string"
Community string for SNMP v1/v2c (default:
.IR public ).
.TP
.BI \-\-version " v1|v2c|v3"
SNMP protocol version (default:
.IR v2c ).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
UDP port of the agent (default:
.IR 161 ).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start against a built\-in synthetic agent; no network access.  TUI only.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " name"
SNMPv3 security name.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " noAuthNoPriv|authNoPriv|authPriv"
SNMPv3 security level.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-proto " MD5|SHA|SHA224|SHA256|SHA384|SHA512"
SNMPv3 authentication protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-pass " string"
SNMPv3 authentication passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-\-priv\-proto " DES|AES|AES192|AES256"
SNMPv3 privacy protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-priv\-pass " string"
SNMPv3 privacy passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-\-context " string"
SNMPv3 context name.
.TP
.BI \-\-communities " a,b,c"
.RB ( discover )
Comma\-separated list of community strings to probe on each host.
.TP
.BI \-\-asn " n"
.RB ( discover )
Resolve every IPv4 prefix announced by AS
.I n
(via the RIPEstat data API) and scan them all.  May take a long time; the sweep
is streamed and can be interrupted.
.TP
.B \-\-local
.RB ( discover )
Scan this host's private interface networks plus the common private LAN
.RI / 24s.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-hosts " n"
.RB ( discover )
Cap on the number of addresses probed in one run (default 262144).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " n"
.RB ( monitor )
Seconds between polls (default 5).
.TP
.B \-\-delta
.RB ( monitor )
Print the per\-second rate for counter values instead of the raw counter.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/snmpdigger/config.yaml
Persisted settings and the most recently used connection profile.  Honours
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the TUI and connect interactively:
.B snmpdigger
.TP
Explore the interface without a device:
.B snmpdigger --demo
.TP
Discover every SNMP host on a subnet:
.B snmpdigger discover 192.168.1.0/24 --community public
.TP
Scan your local networks and everything an AS announces:
.B snmpdigger discover --local
.br
.B snmpdigger discover --asn AS13335 --json
.TP
Walk a subtree from the shell:
.B snmpdigger walk 10.0.0.1 1.3.6.1.2.1.2 --version v2c --community public
.TP
Follow a counter's rate like watch(1):
.B snmpdigger monitor 10.0.0.1 1.3.6.1.2.1.2.2.1.10.2 --delta --interval 2
.TP
Identify a device:
.B snmpdigger identify 10.0.0.1
